13:T435,Combine flour and salt in a large mixing bowl. Make a hole in the center, and pour oil, egg, 1/2 teaspoon lemon juice, and 1 tablespoon orange blossom water into the center. Mix with fingers until the dough resembles coarse crumbs. Gradually sprinkle with warm water while mixing until the dough becomes soft and pliable. Divide into 4 equal portions. Cover dough with a wet cloth, and set aside. In a food processor, finely grind the almonds. Measure 3 cups of the finely ground almonds into a mixing bowl, and stir together with 1 cup sugar, baking powder, vanilla powder, lemon zest, and 2 tablespoons orange flower water. Mix in three eggs one at a time, stirring constantly; mix until you get a sticky, paste-like mixture. Incorporate 2 cups all purpose flour, 2 tbsp vegetable oil, 1 whole egg, 0.5 tsp lemon juice, 1 pinch salt, 1 tbsp orange blossom water, 4 cups almonds, 1 cup sugar, 3 whole egg, 0.5 tsp baking powder, 1 tsp vanilla, 1 zest of 1 lemon, 2 tbsp orange blossom water, 1 sprinkling cornstarch, and 1 to serve pine nuts smoothly until evenly distributed.11:["$","noscript",null,{"children":["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Dziriat (Algerian Almond Tarts)"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Algerian-inspired dziriat (algerian almond tarts) with 19 measured ingredients — zero sign-up, instant Cook Mode. Ready in 45 mins (6 servings). 4.9★ rated with US/Metric scaling & hands-free Cook Mode."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Ingredients"}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","0",{"children":"1 cup Sugar"}],["$","li","1",{"children":"1 cup Water"}],["$","li","2",{"children":"1 tsp Lemon Juice"}],["$","li","3",{"children":"2 tbsp Orange Blossom Water"}],["$","li","4",{"children":"2 cups All purpose flour"}],["$","li","5",{"children":"2 tbsp Vegetable Oil"}],["$","li","6",{"children":"1 whole Egg"}],["$","li","7",{"children":"0.5 tsp Lemon Juice"}],["$","li","8",{"children":"1 pinch Salt"}],["$","li","9",{"children":"1 tbsp Orange Blossom Water"}],["$","li","10",{"children":"4 cups Almonds"}],["$","li","11",{"children":"1 cup Sugar"}],["$","li","12",{"children":"3 whole Egg"}],["$","li","13",{"children":"0.5 tsp Baking Powder"}],["$","li","14",{"children":"1 tsp Vanilla"}],["$","li","15",{"children":"1 zest of 1 Lemon"}],["$","li","16",{"children":"2 tbsp Orange Blossom Water"}],["$","li","17",{"children":"1 sprinkling Cornstarch"}],["$","li","18",{"children":"1 to serve Pine Nuts"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Step-by-Step Instructions"}],["$","ol",null,{"children":[["$","li","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Simmer & Dissolve Smoothly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Prepare the almonds the day before. Bring 6 cups of water to a boil. Remove from heat, and add the almonds. Let the almonds soak in water for about 5 minutes, then drain and peel. Spread the almonds on baking sheets, and bake at 200 degrees F(95 degrees C) until completely dry and toasted. This takes several hours, and needs to be prepared ahead. Be careful not to burn the nuts, as this will give a bitter taste to the filling. Combine 1 cup sugar and 1 cup water in a saucepan, and bring to a boil. Add 1 teaspoon lemon juice, reduce heat to low, and let it simmer until syrupy, about 30 to 40 minutes. Stir in orange blossom water, and remove from heat. Set sugar syrup aside. Incorporate 1 cup sugar, 1 cup water, 1 tsp lemon juice, and 2 tbsp orange blossom water smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"$13"}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Bake Dziriat (Algerian Almond Tarts) & Check Doneness"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Bake for 30 minutes until the edges turn golden and set while the center remains tender. Test with a toothpick—if it comes out with a few moist crumbs rather than wet batter, it is ready."}]]}],"$L14"]}],"$L15"]}]}]
